        "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity",
        "problem": "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = -6t-3t^2$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t$.",
        "worked_solution": "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6-6t \\\\  & =-6(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
